{
  "comment": "Import mapping for Wilkinson Audio's Naked Drums, in kinwie's SFZ conversion (sfzinstruments/WilkinsonAudio.NakedDrums). The stereo-out program is read with every mic layer on. Its sample names don't say which drum a file belongs to (the kick-in and snare-bottom mics share one name, as do the kick-sub and first snare-top mics, and all five tom mics), so those mics are identified by the codes at the end of the file names, taken from the SFZ's own group files; the rest by name. The 'China Wide OH' mic is a stereo pair over the cymbals. Choke keys (60-66) aren't imported: cymbals are choked by their choke notes or aftertouch.",
